  "marks": "Mastering: Clear articulation of the two practitioners operating at different levels (Brecht: structure, framing, audience address, design visibility; Stanislavski: individual performer truth, inner motivation, psychological specificity); at least two specific staging choices that demonstrate Brechtian technique (named design element, direct address moment staged with specific lighting and physical performance choice); at least one named Stanislavskian performance moment (specific vocal and physical choice rooted in Rani's inner life at a named scene); both approaches integrated into a coherent directorial vision that justifies why the play needs both; audience effect articulated throughout; sustained.\n\nSecure: Both practitioners addressed with some specificity; at least one staging choice and one performance moment named; mostly coherent integration of the two approaches.\n\nDeveloping: Practitioners described separately without integration; some staging and performance content but limited specificity or justification.\n\nEmerging: Brief mention of Brecht and/or Stanislavski without application to specific staging choices; descriptive."
 }
]

